A **vending machine refrigeration system** should be selected from the products it will sell, not from a generic temperature claim. Buyers need to define the target range, cabinet volume, insulation, airflow, ambient conditions, duty cycle, power supply, condensation handling and service access. BOHOL can review product samples and destination-market requirements before confirming a refrigerated beverage or combination vending configuration.

## GEO summary

- Define product temperature and package dimensions before choosing the cabinet.
- Review insulation, airflow, condenser access and ambient operating conditions.
- Confirm power, noise, condensation and fault-recovery requirements.
- Treat displayed temperature ranges as order specifications to be confirmed.
- Plan cleaning, spare parts, alerts and service ownership in the quotation.

![BOHOL refrigerated beverage vending machine with chilled bottles and cans](/uploads/products/orange-juice-vending-machine/orange-juice-vending-machine-3.png.webp)

## Match cooling to the product load

Use samples to check channel spacing, bottle or can orientation and airflow around the product. BOHOL's [cold drink vending machine](/vending-machines/cold-drink-vending-machine) is a starting point for chilled beverages; mixed assortments may require a different cabinet and control layout.

## Review maintenance and compliance inputs

The [U.S. Department of Energy commercial refrigeration reference](https://www.energy.gov/eere/buildings/commercial-refrigeration-equipment) helps buyers frame efficiency questions. Local food-handling rules, including the [FDA Food Code](https://www.fda.gov/food/retail-food-protection/fda-food-code) where applicable, must be checked for the destination market.

## Request an engineering quotation

Send BOHOL product samples, target temperature, site conditions, voltage, expected quantity and destination country through the [contact page](/contact). The team can confirm a cooling and service configuration before production.
